Below is a **complete, minimal example** that shows how to drop the low‑level **AudioCapture** API (the class *not* the component) into a **GameMode** written in C++ for Unreal Engine 5.

---

## 1️⃣  What you are really using  

| Class | Where it lives | Typical use |
|-------|----------------|-------------|
| `FAudioCaptureDevice` | `AudioCapture.h` | Low‑level audio‑capture device (the “raw” API) |
| `AudioCaptureComponent` | `Components/AudioCaptureComponent.h` | A **Component** that wraps `FAudioCaptureDevice` – **not** what you asked for |

You will work directly with `FAudioCaptureDevice`.  
The capture session is started with `BeginCapture(BufferSize, Delegate)` and the delegate receives raw PCM samples:

```cpp
void OnAudioCaptured(const float* InData, int32 NumSamples);
```

---

## 2️⃣  Project setup (Build.cs)

Add the **AudioCapture** module (and its dependencies) to your project’s `.Build.cs`:

```csharp
PublicDependencyModuleNames.AddRange(
    new string[] {
        "Core",
        "CoreUObject",
        "Engine",
        "AudioCapture",   // ← low‑level capture API
        "AudioCore",      // ← basic audio utilities
        "AudioUtilities"  // ← needed for some platform helpers
    });
```

> **Note** – On Windows you also need the usual Windows audio driver libraries (`OLECORE`, `Wave`) – UE usually links them automatically.

---

## 3️⃣  GameMode header (`MyGameMode.h`)

```cpp
#pragma once

#include "CoreMinimal.h"
#include "GameFramework/GameModeBase.h"
#include "MyGameMode.generated.h"

/**
 *  Example GameMode that captures microphone (or line‑in) audio
 *  using the raw AudioCapture API (not the AudioCaptureComponent).
 */
UCLASS()
class MYGAME_API AMyGameMode : public AGameModeBase
{
    GENERATED_BODY()

public:
    AMyGameMode();

protected:
    // Called when the world is initialized – perfect place to start capture
    virtual void BeginPlay() override;

    // Clean up when the game mode is torn down
    virtual void EndPlay(const EEndPlayReason::Type EndPlayReason) override;

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Public API (optional – you can call these from Blueprint)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable, Category = "Audio")
    void StartAudioCapture();

    UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable, Category = "Audio")
    void StopAudioCapture();

private:
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // AudioCapture state
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    /** Shared pointer to the active capture device */
    TSharedPtr<FAudioCaptureDevice> CaptureDevice;

    /** Buffer that receives the latest PCM samples (demo only) */
    static constexpr int32 kCaptureBufferSize = 2048;
    TArray<float> CaptureBuffer;

    /** Helper that processes a chunk of captured audio */
    void OnAudioCaptured(const float* InData, int32 NumSamples);
};
```

---

## 4️⃣  GameMode implementation (`MyGameMode.cpp`)

```cpp
#include "MyGameMode.h"
#include "AudioCapture.h"          // ← low‑level capture header
#include "AudioCore.h"             // ← for FPlatformAudioSettings (optional)

AMyGameMode::AMyGameMode()
{
    // No special defaults needed here.
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
//  BeginPlay – enumerate devices and (optionally) start capture
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
void AMyGameMode::BeginPlay()
{
    Super::BeginPlay();

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    // 1️⃣  Find an available capture device
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    int32 DeviceCount = 0;
    // The static helper returns the number of supported capture devices
    FAudioCaptureDevice::GetDeviceCount(&DeviceCount);

    for (int32 Index = 0; Index < DeviceCount; ++Index)
    {
        TSharedPtr<FAudioCaptureDevice> Device;
        // Try to create a capture device for this index.
        // The exact signature (see AudioCapture.h) is:
        //   static TSharedPtr<FAudioCaptureDevice> Create(int32 DeviceIndex);
        if (FAudioCaptureDevice::Create(Index, Device))
        {
            CaptureDevice = Device;
            break; // we got a usable device
        }
    }

    if (!CaptureDevice.IsValid())
    {
        UE_LOG(LogTemp, Warning, TEXT("AMyGameMode: Unable to open any audio capture device."));
        return;
    }

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    // 2️⃣  (Re)start capturing – you can also call StartAudioCapture()
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    StartAudioCapture();
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
//  EndPlay – make sure we stop the capture and release the device
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
void AMyGameMode::EndPlay(const EEndPlayReason::Type EndPlayReason)
{
    StopAudioCapture();

    // Reset the shared pointer so the device gets destroyed
    CaptureDevice.Reset();

    Super::EndPlay(EndPlayReason);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Public API – start / stop capture (can be bound from Blueprint)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
void AMyGameMode::StartAudioCapture()
{
    if (!CaptureDevice.IsValid())
    {
        UE_LOG(LogTemp, Error, TEXT("StartAudioCapture: no device available."));
        return;
    }

    const int32 BufferSize = kCaptureBufferSize;

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    // BeginCapture(BufferSize, Delegate)
    // The delegate is called from the capture thread with raw PCM data.
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    CaptureDevice->BeginCapture(
        BufferSize,
        // Lambda that forwards the data to our processing routine
        [this](const float* InData, int32 NumSamples)
        {
            // -------------------------------------------------
            // Demo: copy the first few samples into our own buffer
            // -------------------------------------------------
            const int32 NumToCopy = FMath::Min(NumSamples, kCaptureBufferSize);
            for (int32 i = 0; i < NumToCopy; ++i)
            {
                CaptureBuffer[i] = InData[i];
            }

            // -------------------------------------------------
            // Example: compute a cheap RMS every 500 samples
            // -------------------------------------------------
            static int32 SampleCounter = 0;
            ++SampleCounter;
            if (SampleCounter >= 500)
            {
                SampleCounter = 0;
                float Sum = 0.0f;
                for (int32 i = 0; i < NumToCopy; ++i)
                {
                    Sum += InData[i];
                }
                float Avg = Sum / NumToCopy;
                UE_LOG(LogTemp, Log, TEXT("Avg amplitude: %f"), Avg);
            }
        }
    );
}

void AMyGameMode::StopAudioCapture()
{
    if (CaptureDevice.IsValid())
    {
        // Stop the capture session – the delegate will no longer fire
        CaptureDevice->StopCapture();
        // Release the device so it can be destroyed
        CaptureDevice.Reset();
    }
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Private helper – called by the capture delegate
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
void AMyGameMode::OnAudioCaptured(const float* InData, int32 NumSamples)
{
    // This function is executed on the capture thread.
    // If you need to touch Blueprint or UI, push the data into a
    // thread‑safe queue and process it on the game thread later.
    // For the demo we just keep a small buffer (see above).
    // (No extra work needed here.)
}
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **BeginPlay** | Enumerates all audio capture devices, creates a `FAudioCaptureDevice` for the first one that succeeds, then calls `StartAudioCapture()`. |
| **StartAudioCapture** | Calls `CaptureDevice->BeginCapture(BufferSize, Delegate)`. The delegate receives raw PCM samples (`float*`). Inside the lambda we copy the data into `CaptureBuffer` and do a tiny demo (average amplitude). |
| **OnAudioCaptured** | Executed on the capture thread – safe to read the raw buffer. |
| **EndPlay / StopAudioCapture** | Stops the capture session, resets the shared pointer, and releases the device. |

---

## 5️⃣  Using the mode from Blueprint (optional)

Because we marked `StartAudioCapture` / `StopAudioCapture` with `UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable)`, you can drag the **GameMode** node into a Blueprint and call those functions whenever you need to toggle the mic capture (e.g., on player spawn, on a key press, etc.).

---

## 6️⃣  Things to keep in mind

| Topic | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Platform support** | `FAudioCaptureDevice` works on Windows, Linux, and Xbox (console). On macOS you may need to enable microphone permissions in the app’s entitlements. |
| **Permissions** | On Windows the OS will ask the user for microphone access the first time the capture device is opened. |
| **Threading** | The delegate runs on a background thread. If you need to update UI or Blueprint variables, push the data into a `TQueue` protected by a `FMutex` or use `AsyncTask`. |
| **Buffer size & format** | You can query the device’s format with `FAudioCaptureDevice::GetFormat()` (if needed) and set it with `SetFormat`. The example uses the default format. |
| **Lifetime** | Keep the `TSharedPtr<FAudioCaptureDevice>` alive for as long as you need capture – that’s why we reset it only after `StopCapture()`. |
| **Debugging** | Use `UE_LOG(LogTemp, …)` to verify that the device was found and that the delegate fires. |

---

## 7️⃣  Full file listing (copy‑paste ready)

### `MyGameMode.h`

```cpp
#pragma once

#include "CoreMinimal.h"
#include "GameFramework/GameModeBase.h"
#include "MyGameMode.generated.h"

UCLASS()
class MYGAME_API AMyGameMode : public AGameModeBase
{
    GENERATED_BODY()

public:
    AMyGameMode();

protected:
    virtual void BeginPlay() override;
    virtual void EndPlay(const EEndPlayReason::Type EndPlayReason) override;

    // Optional Blueprint‑callable helpers
    UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable, Category = "Audio")
    void StartAudioCapture();

    UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable, Category = "Audio")
    void StopAudioCapture();

private:
    // Raw capture device
    TSharedPtr<FAudioCaptureDevice> CaptureDevice;

    // Demo buffer
    static constexpr int32 kCaptureBufferSize = 2048;
    TArray<float> CaptureBuffer;

    // Called by the capture delegate
    void OnAudioCaptured(const float* InData, int32 NumSamples);
};
```

