| `const dataTestId = element.getAttribute('span');` | Removed – we don’t need any attribute named `span`. Instead we read `element.textContent`. |
| No explicit wait for the element | Added `await page.waitForSelector('[data-testid="prediction_option"]');` before trying to read it. |
| Extraction logic | Replaced with `el.textContent.trim()` which returns the visible text inside the element (the “contents”). |

### How to adapt further

* **If you need an attribute instead of text** – replace the `return el.textContent.trim();` line with something like `return el.getAttribute('someAttribute');`.
* **If the element contains nested tags** – `textContent` still gives you all the inner text; use `innerText` if you prefer the rendered version.
